    "result": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented the threshold feature for `frai eval`. Here's what was added:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n### **Core Changes (frai-core)**\n\n1. **`generateReport` function** \u2013 Now accepts optional `thresholds` object:\n   - Evaluates each threshold against metric scores\n   - Metrics with no score fail their threshold (instead of crashing)\n   - Adds `passed` field (true if all thresholds pass, false if any fail)\n   - Adds `thresholds` array with `{ metric, min, score, passed }` entries\n   - Report structure unchanged when no thresholds provided\n\n2. **Reporters** \u2013 Updated to include threshold outcomes:\n   - **JSON**: Report gains top-level `passed` and `thresholds` list\n   - **Markdown**: Adds \"Thresholds\" section before metrics showing PASS/FAIL for each\n\n3. **Tests** \u2013 Added three new tests covering:\n   - Thresholds that pass\n   - Thresholds that fail\n   - Metrics with no score (exact_match without references)\n\n### **CLI Changes (frai-cli)**\n\n1. **`parseThresholds` function** \u2013 Validates and parses threshold strings:\n   - Format: `metric=value` (0-1)\n   - Returns errors for malformed thresholds, unknown metrics, or invalid ranges\n   - Lists all valid metric IDs in error messages\n\n2. **`--threshold` option** \u2013 Added to `frai eval`:\n   - Can be specified multiple times: `--threshold exact_match=0.9 --threshold toxicity=0.95`\n   - Uses Commander's accumulator callback to collect multiple values\n\n3. **Exit codes**:\n   - **0**: All thresholds pass (or none specified)\n   - **1**: Any threshold fails (report still written)\n   - **2**: Usage error (malformed threshold, unknown metric, invalid value)\n\n4. **Report writing** \u2013 Always writes the report regardless of pass/fail, includes outcome details\n\n### **Documentation**\n\nUpdated `README.md` with complete `--threshold` usage and examples.\n\n## Backward Compatibility\n\n\u2713 Without `--threshold`, behavior is unchanged (exit 0 always, report written as before)  \n\u2713 Existing SDK users can pass `thresholds` object to `generateReport`  \n\u2713 All existing tests remain passing (plus new threshold tests)\n\nThe implementation handles all edge cases: metrics with no score fail thresholds, missing references are detected, and validation errors exit 2 as expected.",
